      "title": "The documentary camera",
      "notes": [
        "Leave the page alone for 18 seconds and the camera takes over: it zooms in and pans between whatever is most interesting (bots with something to say, pairs deep in conversation, crowds around a fire, cooking and crafting), staying on each for 7 seconds, with an occasional wide shot. Touch anything and you're back in control.",
        "The stats moved below the canvas. A same-night follow-up made the camera work on phones by moving the view with CSS transforms instead of scrolling (commits 426fa65 + 5e8a735)."
      ],
      "known": [
        "Same seed doesn't give the same world: the fire and decay passes walk HashMaps in random order.",
        "A forest tile can mature into a tree under a bot standing on it, trapping the bot.",
        "No births: the population only ever shrinks. Berries never rot, and stockpiles reach hundreds.",
